 and the QC for \"proper pairs\": report bowtie2's FLAG 0x2 count with a caveat that the -X default of 500 bp truncates concordance, and that library statistics are computed directly from spans.\n\nAlso, the report should include a per-100 kb depth table for the region of interest, plus a genome-wide summary. Keep qc.json focused.\n\nNow the size: exact_size = q - p - 1 = 21,000,001 - 20,000,000 - 1 = 1,000,000 ✓. First-deleted position = p+1 = 20,000,001; last-deleted position = q-1 = 21,000,000. Rounded: round(20,000,001/100000)*100000 = 20,000,000; round(21,000,000/100000)*100000 = 21,000,000. size_bp for TSV: use end_100kb - start_100kb = 1,000,000 ✓ (equal to exact here).\n\nSupporting signals string (TSV-safe, semicolon-separated):\n`read_depth_zero_bins=10;read_depth_baseline=2.68x;depth_inside=0.05x;split_reads=3;junction=20000000|21000001;discordant_pairs=2;pair_spans=1000563/1000492;insert_median=467`\n\nReport.md sections:\n1. Summary\n2. Input data and methods\n3. QC\n4. Evidence for the deletion (depth / split reads / spanning pairs / zygosity)\n5. Coordinate precision: evidence vs. reporting rounding\n6. Regions considered and rejected (segmental-duplication artifacts, N-gap confounders)\n7. Limitations\n8. Reproducibility (how to run analysis.py)\n\nAlright, write the complete final analysis.py in one here-string with correct syntax. Must avoid `'@` at the beginning of a line within the content (none) and keep the terminator at column 0.\n\nActually, given the size, maybe it's safer to write the file with two appends (part1/part2) using Set-Content/Add-Content with -Value $code. Let me carefully compose the full script in my head and write it in two chunks.\n\nChunk size: keep each here-string under ~8–10k characters for command reliability. The full script is probably 18–20k characters. Do it in three chunks."}}
