\nFurther recheck: does analysis.py depend on files inside tools/ other than the bowtie2 binaries? find_bowtie2 scans subdirectories under tools/ — only the bowtie2 directory remains. Good.\n\nEdge case: the junction scan opens work/r1.fq and r2.fq (uncompressed). Good.\n\nLet me also confirm that the TSV is tab-separated, and check the final file list. Then, clean up.\n\nAlso, is it worth verifying that the numbers in qc.json are consistent with the earlier manual exploration? Yes:\n- pairs_both=332120, single=3 ✓\n- FR=328008, RF=1147, same_strand=2965 ✓ (matches)\n- insert median 499/MAD 29 (over the span 100–2000 population — a slightly different definition than the earlier proper-pair-only 467/20; documented) ✓\n- baseline 2.742 ✓, mean depth 2.681 ✓\n- residual inside the deletion 0.0458x, ratio 1.7% ✓\n- zero bins list ✓ (10 bins)\n- junction reads ✓, spanning pairs ✓ (inferred fragment lengths 565/494 — hmm, inferred_fragment is calculated as span - exact_size = 1,000,563 - 1,000,000 = 563? Wait, in qc it's 565. Check: implied_fragment = span - (right_guess - left_guess - 1). In main() spans is computed with left_guess/right_guess (20,000,001/21,000,000): right_guess - left_guess - 1 = 21,000,000 - 20,000,001 - 1 = 999,998. So inferred value = 1,000,563 - 999,998 = 565. Slightly off from the true D=1,000,000 → inferred value = span - 999,998 = F + 2. Minor inconsistency: the estimate of the deleted length used for inference should be exact_size. The difference is 2 bp — negligible, but let me fix it for consistency: implied_fragment = span - exact_size. Patch: compute spans after exact_size is determined... currently spans is computed before consolidation. Simplest way: when writing qc, recalculate the implied fragment with exact_size: s['span'] - exact_size. Patch spanning_pairs() to take del_size as a parameter... or just adjust in main after consolidation: for s in spans: s['implied_fragment'] = s['span'] - exact_size. Add this small patch.)\n\nPatch that